    <title>Machine Learning 01</title>
    <link href="http://example.com/2025/11/20/01/"/>
    <id>http://example.com/2025/11/20/01/</id>
    <published>2025-11-20T13:05:02.000Z</published>
    <updated>2025-11-20T13:20:29.741Z</updated>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Machine Learning algorithms</p><ul><li>supervised learnning, used most</li><li>unsupervised learning</li><li>recommender systems</li><li>reinforcement learing</li></ul><h1 id="notation"><a href="#notation" class="headerlink" title="notation"></a>notation</h1><ul><li>x &#x3D; ‘input’ variable &#x2F; feature</li><li>y &#x3D; ‘output’ variable &#x2F; ‘target’ variable</li><li>m &#x3D; number of traing example</li><li>(x, y) &#x3D; single traing example</li><li>$(x^{i}, y^{i}) &#x3D; i^{th}$ training example $(1^{st}, 2^{nd}, 3^{rd}, …)$</li></ul><h1 id="supervised-learning"><a href="#supervised-learning" class="headerlink" title="supervised learning"></a>supervised learning</h1><ul><li><p>give the system a pair of X label and Y label, after learning ,the system will learn how to give a resonably accurate prediction of the output. Learning input-output or x-to-y mappings.</p></li><li><p>Regression algorithm</p><ul><li>Predict a number from infinitely many possible numbers.</li><li>Linear Regression model<ul><li>function e.g. f(x) &#x3D; wx + b</li></ul></li></ul></li><li><p>Classification algorithm</p><ul><li>classification predicts a small. finite, limited set of possible output catagories.</li><li>classification model predicts categories or discrete categories</li></ul></li></ul><h1 id="unsupervised-learning"><a href="#unsupervised-learning" class="headerlink" title="unsupervised learning"></a>unsupervised learning</h1><ul><li><p>find some structure or some pattern, not asked to give some quote right answer</p></li><li><p>clustering algorithm</p><ul><li>takes data without labels and tries to automatically group them into clusters.</li><li>group similar data together</li></ul></li><li><p>anomaly detection</p><ul><li>find unusual data points</li></ul></li><li><p>dimensionality reduction</p><ul><li>compress data , with losing as little information as possible</li></ul></li></ul>]]></content>
    
    
    <summary type="html">study notes</summary>
    
    
    
